  "plot_summary": "Nine graded stories this month, spread over eight issues (two again from Strange Tales), with a final weighted average of x.xx,\n\nwhich is about a point-and-a-quarter improvement over the previous month's x.xx,\n\nmeaning that, for the most part, the stories this time around were <i>well</i> above just the reader level, and in fact, 4 of the 9 stories were actually at mid-grade or above.&nbsp; It's clear from the letters coming in that there is an overall sense of excitement growing in the readership over the direction of the books in general.\n\nThe improved characterization of the X-Men was a noticeable plus this month, and the Hulk/Sub-Mariner \"super-villain team-up\" was solid also, and Electro's introduction was another in the positive column.&nbsp; While there was nothing really wrong with the FF, it and the other solo tales of Thor, Giant-Man and Iron Man did not elevate up enough into the realm of memorable, and on the negative side, the <i>lame</i> Human Torch and Doctor Strange offerings really make me wonder why I'm reading them at all!",
